write('RECEIPT.json',{decision:'HOLD_FINAL_ACTIVATION',atUTC:new Date(now).toISOString(),packet:{path:author+'/FINAL-PACKET.json',bytes:23330,sha256:hash(packetRaw)},checks,controls:4,sourceInputs:309,emissions:1012,packageMembers:1014,packageQualification:'authenticated producer1014-member inventory and compressed package bytes/hash; no fresh inflate/parse',regularTools,toolLinks:links,runtimeFiles:45,publisherFiles:5,preimportFiles:1,reviews:reviews.map(({receipt,...pin})=>pin),absent,window:{issued:packet.issuedUTC,latestStart:packet.latestStartUTC,expires:packet.expiresUTC,remainingAtCheckMs:Date.parse(packet.expiresUTC)-now},commands:{runtime:packet.runtimeCommand,preimport:packet.preimportCommand,publication:packet.publicationCommand},slots:packet.slots,bounds:packet.bounds,finding,shapeQualification,qualifications:['author preparation peak3 exceeded authorized2; historical compliance HOLD remains, never amended','this prospective identity reauthentication does not repair author run or grant runtime authority','PUBLIC runtime-bound encoded fixture/engine receipts hashed only; no decoding/origin/load-trace/engine execution','trusted Git internal physical storage remains outside measured logical-work budget','future measured6..26 retired starts plus helper self yields7..27; coordinator must observe helper exit/close, no intervening starts; slot still UNMEASURED','window enforcement external; all actual grant/root/work slots absent at check; no renewal or reuse']});
write('REPORT.md',`# B1 v4 independent final-slot review\n\n**HOLD final activation.** Four original PURE identity controls pass, and fresh309 source/1012 emitted files, authenticated1014-member producer inventory/package2fe,2274 regular tools+12links,45 runtime/5 publisher/1preimport pins and both independent acceptance receipts matched. No product/Worker/compiler/install/native execution.\n\n## F01: future preimport still has the nested-array defect\n\n${finding.path}:${finding.line}\n\n\`\`\`js\n${buggy}\n\`\`\`\n\nBound hash ${finding.sha256}. Preparation correctly uses ...preimportFiles, but the future helper has five publisher records followed by one ARRAY. The sixth iteration reads undefined entry.path and calls fs.lstatSync(undefined); source catch maps the error to78 before writing PUBLICATION-AUTHORITY-v3.json. This is source/DATA proof, not an actual preimport run or product failure. A minimal separately versioned helper/packet rebind and different review are required before ROOT can consider actual GO.\n\nThe identity validator's Object.keys also does not enforce absence of hidden/symbol own keys; its four controls establish the narrower tested enumerable-own-data profile, not all-own-key exactness.\n\n## Authority and accounting\nIssued ${packet.issuedUTC}; latest start ${packet.latestStartUTC}; expiry ${packet.expiresUTC}. All12 actual slots remained absent at ${new Date(now).toISOString()}, but freshness is not authority and does not override F01. Exact commands/typed runtime-derived hash and measured-role slots are in RECEIPT.json. Publication count must use actually observed prior6..26 retired starts plus helper self, not reservations/zero. Future32-knownOS/peak3/1800s/64MiBcapture/768MiBlogical-work bounds unchanged; trusted Git internal disk is outside that logical accounting.\n\nAuthor preparation peak3/authorized2 stays historical HOLD. This independent peak3 grant cannot amend it. Old draft windows/undefined-path failure remain preserved. No actual authorization issued. Known roles planned through this publication20 (including two instruction-only readers, four metadata readers, patches, syntax, Git and one PURE helper), direct peak2 within3. No universal transitive census claim.\n`);
